From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fe13 <engine@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 03:22:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/21] core: Fire Emblem: Awakening's scenes from its screen
 markers (EUR and USA)

game_ui.rs holds Awakening's screen markers and the places of its battle
panels, battle buttons, banners, title and world-map pieces; scenes.rs turns
the markers drawn each frame into scenes (battle, forecast, talk, unit view,
world map, title, cursor on a unit, unit picked). System answers the
frontend's questions about them and gives the bottom screen's picture.

Both releases are known: EUR 000400000009F100 and USA 00040000000A0500
(same English UI textures and layout). Nothing is watched unless
Config::game_screens is on (default off), or set_game_screens turns it on.

Adapted from fe-awakening-recomp 832fe86 (github.com/Zelkin1/fe-awakening-recomp,
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 the authors of the Fire Emblem: Awakening
recompilation project): game_ui.rs and scenes.rs, the scene methods of
System in lib.rs, the marker set-up in loader.rs. Changed: the USA title
id, the Config::game_screens switch, set_game_screens.
